{"name":"Blackjack","hex":"#51504d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blackjack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fan of the South Korean girl group 2NE1."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blackjack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackjack","blocks":[{"text":"Blackjack is a casino banking game. It is the most widely played casino banking game in the world. It uses decks of 52 cards and descends from a global family of casino banking games known as \"twenty-one\". This family of card games also includes the European games vingt-et-un and pontoon, and the Russian game Ochko. The game is a comparing card game where players compete against the dealer, rather than each other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/BlackJackGame.jpg/330px-BlackJackGame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackjack","wikidata":"Q228044"},{"title":"BlackJack (film series)","blocks":[{"text":"BlackJack is a series of Australian television movies created by Shaun Micallef and Gary McCaffrie, and starring Colin Friels. The movies began airing on Network Ten in 2003 and concluded in 2007. They were shown in the United Kingdom on the BBC and UKTV Drama."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Black_Jack_DVD_cover_%28lo_res%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BlackJack_(film_series)","wikidata":"Q2034992"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Blackjack_game_1.JPG/500px-Blackjack_game_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Blackjack_game_1.JPG/1280px-Blackjack_game_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Bl